 "modules": [
  {
   "id": 1,
   "plugin": "Core",
   "model": "Notes",
   "data": {
    "text": "LIGHT & LOOK\nPatch any CV (0 to 10 V) into a jack. 0 V is the item's From setting, 10 V its To.\n\nCV-CC 1: MIDI channel 5, CC 33 to 48\n   1 Key direction\n   2 Contrast\n   3 Color of the light\n   4 Lighting\n   5 Time of day\n   6 Softness\n   7 Rim light\n   8 Sources\n   9 Source in frame\n  10 Shaped light\n  11 Air\n  12 When the light changes\n  13 Brightness key\n  14 Render style\n  15 Ink line\n  16 Gloss\nCV-CC 2: MIDI channel 5, CC 49 to 64\n   1 Wetness\n   2 Light in skin\n   3 Something glows\n   4 Wear\n   5 Color saturation\n   6 Dominant color\n   7 Lighting\n   8 Light setup\n   9 Surfaces and materials\n  10 Skin\n  11 Drawn or real look\n  12 Layers of the picture\n  13 suite: Noir\n  14 suite: Golden hour\n  15 suite: Comic ink\n  16 suite: Wet night\nCV-CC 3: MIDI channel 5, CC 65 to 80\n   1 suite: Clean product\n   2 suite: Neon night\n   3 suite: Candlelit\n   4 suite: Sitcom bright\n   5 suite: Interrogation\n   6 suite: Campfire night\n   7 suite: Warm animated feature\n   8 suite: Magic hour\n   9 suite: Candlelit room\n  10 suite: Neon noir\n  11 pair: When the render goes toon, the ink line is heavy\n  12 pair: When a secret comes out, the face goes half lit\n  13 pair: After a loss, the color drains\n  14 pair: A flashback brings the faded look\n  15 pair: When danger rises, the shadows deepen\n  16 pair: A reunion warms the color\nCV-CC 4: MIDI channel 5, CC 81 to 96\n   1 pair: When the fire grows, faces go warm and red\n   2 pair: When night falls, the light turns to moonlight\n   3 pair: When moonlight takes over, the light turns blue\n   4 pair: When the light goes cold, the characters drift apart\n   5 pair: When the day reaches dusk, the light goes low and golden\n   6 pair: When dusk light is used, the light changes while the shot holds\n   7 pair: When the light shifts during a held shot, the feeling inside grows\n   8 pair: When light glows warm through the skin, the feeling gets stronger\n   9 pair: When a lamp is in the shot, the light seems to come from it\n  10 pair: When the light comes from lamps, it turns warm\n  11 pair: When the light is warm lamplight, the room feels cozy\n  12 pair: When the main light moves to the side, half the face falls into shadow\n  13 pair: When the contrast climbs, the whole picture goes dark\n  14 pair: When the picture goes dark, people hide more than they say\n  15 pair: When haze fills the air, the shaped light shows up as beams\n  16 pair: When blind stripes fall across a face, the tension rises\nCV-CC 5: MIDI channel 5, CC 97 to 112\n   1 pair: When the main light goes behind the actor, a strong edge of light appears\n   2 pair: When a strong edge light outlines the actor, they pop off the background\n   3 pair: When the hair is pale, a thin edge light is enough\n   4 pair: When the street is soaked, every surface turns to a mirror\n   5 pair: When surfaces are mirror-shiny, every lamp appears twice\n   6 pair: When everything looks worn and ruined, the place feels gloomy\n   7 pair: When the colors narrow to one, any other color jumps out\n   8 pair: When an object glows, the eye goes straight to it\n   9 pair: When the light comes from a window, it falls soft across faces\n  10 pair: When the picture looks drawn, the comedy can go cartoon-big\n  11 pair: When the picture goes bright and even, the comedy gets playful\n  12 pair: When the streets are wet at night, the neon glows twice as bright\n  13 pair: When the blinds cut the light into bars, the hero looks trapped\n  14 pairs: Weather and surface\n  15 pairs: Light follows feeling\n  16 pairs: Night comes down\nCV-CC 6: MIDI channel 6, CC 1 to 7\n   1 pairs: The golden hour turn\n   2 pairs: Lamplit closeness\n   3 pairs: Noir squeeze\n   4 pairs: Smoky blinds\n   5 pairs: Halo from behind\n   6 pairs: Wet neon street\n   7 pairs: Neon noir: the moves"
   },
   "pos": [
